{"step_update": {"step_type": "tool", "state": "DONE", "tool_name": "run_command", "tool_info": {"parameters": {"CommandLine": "gh api repos/Crazycatz67/asl-recognizer/branches/main"}, "output": "{\"name\":\"main\",\"commit\":{\"sha\":\"fd29dd06ce6f75eee55bc0e1a98605937218ffe3\",\"node_id\":\"C_kwDOUNXR89oAKGZkMjlkZDA2Y2U2Zjc1ZWVlNTViYzBlMWE5ODYwNTkzNzIxOGZmZTM\",\"commit\":{\"author\":{\"name\":\"Farhan Amin\",\"email\":\"b@example.edu\",\"date\":\"2026-10-01T09:07:08Z\"},\"committer\":{\"name\":\"Farhan Amin\",\"email\":\"b@example.edu\",\"date\":\"2026-10-01T09:07:08Z\"},\"message\":\"Fix G and H reference showing the mirror image of the handshape (#59) — sw.js v112\\n\\nThe owner saw G's reference \\\"mirrored\\\" and wrong. The G and H photos and\\ntheir dataset centroids are mirrored relative to every other letter (same\\nhandedness signature as B: 0 of 170 G samples the other way), so the shared\\npanel flip rule drew them as their own mirror image in every camera/hand\\nsetting, contradicting the \\\"palm facing you, across your body\\\" caption and\\nthe B22 back-of-hand shading. SOURCE_MIRRORED + refPanelMirrored() give G and\\nH the opposite flip. Selfie camera, right hand: G now points across the body\\nwith the back of the hand showing. Read mode and the enlarged views still\\nnever flip (open). selftest 276/0 (#59 check fails 8 cases on the old rule),\\nci-check all passed. Needs a live camera check.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"tree\":{\"sha\":\"52391c60c716835ef7dd7a25def53cc4b87533e5\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/Crazycatz67/asl-recognizer/git/trees/52391c60c716835ef7dd7a25def53cc4b87533e5\"},\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/Crazycatz67/asl-recognizer/git/commits/fd29dd06ce6f75eee55bc0e1a98605937218ffe3\",\"comment_count\":0,\"verification\":{\"verified\":false,\"reason\":\"unsigned\",\"signature\":null,\"payload\":null,\"verified_at\":null}},\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/Crazycatz67/asl-